Web parity reproduced (every branch the web leaf owns):
  • Title "Acknowledge alert" (web Modal title).
  • Optional acknowledged-alert subtitle  ({alertTitle ? <p> : null}).
  • Free-text note  → web shared <Textarea>  (label "Note (optional)", prompt
    "Optional: what's being done?", disabled while submitting, red error border when
    the trimmed note > 1000 chars, maxLength 1050 input clamp).
  • Always-on character hint  ("Up to 1000 characters. Shared in the audit timeline.")
    with the {{max}} interpolation resolved; the note is aria-describedby it.
  • Cancel (ghost) + Acknowledge (primary) → web shared <Button>s; Cancel disabled
    while submitting; Acknowledge disabled when submitting || tooLong and shows the
    in-button busy spinner (web `submitting`).
  • Reset-on-open + focus-the-note-on-open (web useEffect([open]) + textareaRef.focus).
  • handleSubmit guard  (`if (submitting || tooLong) return; onSubmit(trimmed)`) — an
    empty trimmed note is a valid "ack with no note" submission.
  • Web Modal → native .sheet; web focus-trap/dismiss → native sheet semantics
    (medium/large detents + drag indicator on iOS; sized window-sheet on macOS).

i18n keys (all 6 from source, resolved through the P1/S10 facade, English fallback):
  alerts.ack.dialogTitle, alerts.ack.noteLabel, alerts.ack.notePlaceholder,
  alerts.ack.noteHint, alerts.ack.cancel, alerts.ack.submit  (+ native alerts.ack.close)

States note (read the source — no scope drift): the web leaf's only hooks are
`useTranslation` + `useId` (per this prompt's own "Data sources"). It is a CONTROLLED
PRESENTATIONAL dialog with no query/mutation of its own (the ack mutation belongs to
the parent), so the generic async data axis (loading / empty / error / stale / offline)
does not exist in the source and is not invented here. Every state the source DOES own
is reproduced and tested: default(empty) · typed(valid) · too-long(error) · submitting(busy)
· with/without alert subtitle.

Accessibility: dialog container label (title + alert context), header `.isHeader`,
close VoiceOver label, note field label + value + hint (web aria-describedby), error
announced, Cancel/Acknowledge labels. Dynamic Type via Font.TS system ramp; no custom
animation (reduce-motion safe); 44pt targets via TSButton.

